{{!--
  Header toolbar version tag (see GH issue #7). Reuses the `.ids-tag` block
  from tag/tag.css (`Solid` + `Selected` in the design) rather than the
  Select Tag component — Select Tag pulls in list/scrollable-panel/search-field
  CSS for a dropdown menu this bundle already renders itself below.

  GH-101: gated on `page.componentVersion` (always present for a real page),
  never on `page.versions` — Antora's page-composer only computes
  `page.versions` when `component.versions.length > 1`
  (@antora/page-composer build-ui-model.js); a single-version component (e.g.
  `main` alone, no `stable` tag yet) gets `page.versions === undefined`, and
  gating the whole partial on it — the previous behaviour — meant NEITHER
  branch below ever rendered, not even this one. `page.componentVersion` has
  no such gap, so it's the one truth source both branches key off.

  GH-103: the toggle and the single-version badge both get an explicit
  Latest/older-Stable/Prerelease modifier (`header-toolbar__version--latest`/
  `--older`/`--prerelease`, see header.css) — three states, not two: a
  `page.componentVersion.prerelease` truthy always wins (orange); otherwise
  `(eq page.componentVersion page.component.latest)` decides between "the
  current release" (green) and "a real, older stable version" (grey).

  GH-104: `page.componentVersion.latest` is NOT a real field — don't put it
  back. Antora only ever sets a `latest: true` flag on the copies it builds
  for `page.versions` (@antora/page-composer build-ui-model.js), never on
  the raw `componentVersion` descriptor this partial reads, so that check
  was always false and every stable/latest page rendered grey. The identity
  check `(eq page.componentVersion page.component.latest)` — which this
  once was, and was changed away from — is safe specifically in this `else
  if` slot: the `prerelease` branch above it already wins first, so the
  "component has only a prerelease version, and `component.latest` points
  at it" edge case that motivated the original change away from identity
  comparison can no longer reach here. Don't reorder these branches without
  re-checking that.

  `ids-tag--read-only` (DS modifier, tag/tag.css) marks the badge as
  non-interactive — it isn't a button and does nothing on click, so it must
  not pick up `.ids-tag`'s generic hover cursor/colour shift, which would
  otherwise imply an affordance that isn't there. `aria-label` adds the
  "Version" context the bare displayVersion text doesn't carry on its own.
  The label is always the real `displayVersion` Antora computed; nothing
  here synthesises text.
--}}
{{#if page.componentVersion}}
<div class="page-versions">
  {{#if page.versions.[1]}}
  <button type="button" class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid ids-tag--selected header-toolbar__version{{#if page.componentVersion.prerelease}} header-toolbar__version--prerelease{{else if (eq page.componentVersion page.component.latest)}} header-toolbar__version--latest{{else}} header-toolbar__version--older{{/if}} version-menu-toggle" title="Show other versions of page" aria-expanded="false">
    <span class="ids-tag__label">{{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}</span>
    <span class="ids-tag__icon">{{icon "arrows" "chevron-down-outlined"}}</span>
  </button>
  <div class="version-menu">
    {{#each page.versions}}
    {{!--
      GH-103/GH-105: Stable/Prerelease pill semantics apply to every entry in
      the list, not just the reader's own version — a "Latest" pill whenever
      that entry is genuinely Antora's newest (`./latest`) AND not a
      prerelease; a "Prerelease" pill whenever `./prerelease` is set,
      including a prerelease that also happens to be latest (there being no
      stable version yet). An older, non-latest stable version gets no pill
      at all — "Latest" would be wrong on it, and there is no dedicated
      "Stable" pill in the design (Figma 5SAtxqb5sdtIqDQzz70yts#2610-32852).
      Previously this was only wired into the current-page `<span>` branch,
      so e.g. viewing 0.1.0 would fail to mark 0.2.0 as "Latest" in the list
      — GH-105. Both branches below must carry it identically.
    --}}
    {{#if (eq ./version @root.page.version)}}
    {{!-- the reader's own version: a `<span>`, not a link — nothing to navigate to. --}}
    <span class="version is-current" aria-current="page">
      <span class="version__label">{{./displayVersion}}</span>
      {{#if ./prerelease}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--orange"><span class="ids-label__content">Prerelease</span></span>
      {{else if ./latest}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--green"><span class="ids-label__content">Latest</span></span>
      {{/if}}
    </span>
    {{else}}
    <a class="version{{#if ./missing}} is-missing{{/if}}" href="{{{relativize ./url}}}">
      <span class="version__label">{{./displayVersion}}</span>
      {{#if ./prerelease}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--orange"><span class="ids-label__content">Prerelease</span></span>
      {{else if ./latest}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--green"><span class="ids-label__content">Latest</span></span>
      {{/if}}
    </a>
    {{/if}}
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{else}}
  <span class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid ids-tag--selected ids-tag--read-only header-toolbar__version{{#if page.componentVersion.prerelease}} header-toolbar__version--prerelease{{else if (eq page.componentVersion page.component.latest)}} header-toolbar__version--latest{{else}} header-toolbar__version--older{{/if}}" aria-label="Version {{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}">
    <span class="ids-tag__label">{{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}</span>
  </span>
  {{/if}}
</div>
{{/if}}
